{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-27T22:55:59.519Z","data":{"text":"Done. Both the task verify and the proposal verify pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the \"landed copy counted once\" fix within scope:\n\n**`src/core/status/landed-copies.ts`** (new) — `filterLandedCopies(root, changes)` drops a worktree/stacked tree's archived or rejected folder when the project-root tree holds the same folder in the same location. Active folders are never dropped.\n\n**`src/core/status/change-locations.ts`** — `listChanges` now runs each named tree's entries through `filterLandedCopies(trees[0], own)`. `changeTrees` is untouched. File is 247 lines (under the 250 cap).\n\n**`src/core/run/squash-message.ts`** — `buildSquashMessage` no longer goes through `listChanges`; it resolves matching worktree trees via `changeTrees` and checks their active/archive directories directly, so a checkout that already holds the archive after `git merge --squash` still messages the branch's copy. All refusal messages are unchanged.\n\n**`tests/change-locations-landed.test.ts`** (new) — covers both new \"Change locations\" scenarios through `listChanges`/`changeTrees`, \"Landed change counted once\" through `queueCommand`, `statusCommand`, `inboxCommand --json`, `inboxDispatchCommand --json`, and `reportCommand --json`, and \"Checkout already holds the archive\" through `messageCommand`. I confirmed the tests fail without the resolver fix.\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/104-archived-once/.run/results/1.md`.\n\n`pnpm verify` exits 0 (typechecks, build, full suite, lint)."}}
